    },
    "message": "fix(output-tokens): floor the context-headroom bound instead of emitting a 3-token budget\n\nLatent, not an active failure. The live server log shows only sane values\ntoday -- MAX TOKENS BOUNDED BY CONTEXT producing 42,992-46,128 on\nopencode/hy3-free against 142-146k prompts, and 42,992 is the smallest value\nproduced anywhere. Nothing shipped a tiny max_tokens. The defect is that\nnothing prevented one.\n\nMechanism. _apply_context_headroom, shipped in 5.63.0, computes\n\n    headroom = context_length - input_tokens - context_margin\n\nand returns it whenever 0 < headroom < resolved. That expression is bounded\nbelow by 1, not by anything useful. When a catalogue context_length is wrong,\nor simply small against a long prompt, it emits an arbitrarily small budget --\n3 is reachable. A request carrying max_tokens: 3 does not fail; it succeeds and\nreturns a one-token answer, which reads as \"the model had nothing to say\"\nrather than \"the published context length is wrong\". That is strictly worse\nthan failing. 1,117 of 7,440 models.dev entries report limit.output ==\nlimit.context, so this path is not exotic; it is safe today only by the luck of\ncatalogue quality.\n\nFix. A new MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS_CONTEXT_FLOOR = 4096, declared the way its three\n5.63.0 neighbours are: constants.py default, settings.py with validation_alias,\n.env.example, README table, LIMIT_RANGES bound, and the limits admin manifest\nsection. Below the floor the request is left unmodified and a WARNING names the\nmodel, the context length, the input tokens, the computed headroom and the\nfloor -- the same outcome the headroom <= 0 branch already takes and documents,\nso the provider reports the real context error instead of MCC inventing a\nuseless budget. 0 restores the pre-floor behaviour.\n\nWhy 4,096. Large enough that a surviving request is actually useful: it is the\nentire output limit many catalogue entries publish, and the smallest context\nwindow in the catalogue, so a model handed 4,096 output tokens is asked for no\nless than a real small model can do. Small enough not to reject workable\nrequests: it is a quarter of REASONING_ANSWER_FLOOR_MAX (16,384), which is the\n*most* the reasoning split ever reserves for the visible answer and is applied\nas min(that, output // 2). A floor at or near 16,384 would reject prompts the\nreasoning path itself is content to run at 2,048 answer tokens; a quarter\nleaves that split its full working range while still refusing the arbitrarily\nsmall budgets the floor exists to stop.\n\nThe four decision steps stay separately named as 5.63.0 left them\n(_apply_model_limit, _fall_back_when_unknown, _apply_ceiling,\n_apply_context_headroom). Behaviour at headroom <= 0 and headroom >= resolved\nis untouched.\n\nVerification.\n\n    $ uv run ty check\n    All checks passed!\n\n    $ uv run pytest -q --tb=line\n    14 failed, 5697 passed, 38 skipped in 177.05s (0:02:57)\n\nThe 14 are the known baseline: 8 websearch tests reading the real ~/.fcc/.env\nand 6 PowerShell installer tests. None are in files this commit touches.\n\n    $ uv run pytest tests/application/test_output_tokens.py \\\n        tests/config/test_admin_limits.py tests/config/test_limit_bounds.py -q\n    339 passed in 15.70s\n\nNew tests pin: the live-shaped case (131,072 context, 100,000 prompt -> 30,048,\nstill bounded exactly as before); a positive headroom of 3 leaving the request\nunmodified with the WARNING naming model, context, input, headroom and floor;\nheadroom exactly at the floor still sent; a floor of 0 restoring the old\nbehaviour; and the env override plus the shipped default. The existing contract\npairing the admin manifest default to the settings default now covers the new\nkey.\n\nNot done. The ~22 NoReasoning provider profiles and the echo-susceptible\nsubstring matching in mistral/reasoning.py and deepseek/tool_choice.py are out\nof scope and unchanged.\n\nVersion 5.69.2 -> 5.69.3 (PATCH) with uv.lock.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016Rsc8AeKxx8h6zFwfT9sD4",
